-- A loan belongs to one member. A member has a loan when a Loan exists for it. Rule MoveLoan
-- gives a loan to another member when a Transfer arrives, by setting the loan's `member`.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes", exactly one line about MemberWithLoan:
--
--   ### Member
--   - A new Loan can now make a Member become a MemberWithLoan.
--
-- Two lines are missing. Moving a member's only loan makes its receiver a MemberWithLoan and
-- makes the member it left stop being one. The same condition spelled `exists loans` or
-- `exists (Loan where member == this)` draws both lines. The compiler does not record which
-- field of Loan `for this` matched, so a write of `Loan.member` is not seen as a change.
act Member { name: text }

act Loan {
    member: one Member
    dueOn: Date
}

transient act Transfer {
    loan: one Loan
    receiver: one Member
}

rule MoveLoan when Transfer {
    loan.member = receiver
}

shape MemberWithLoan = Member where exists Loan for this
